	(text "USB-C input, logic supply, fan supply, isolated analog supply"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 4.0 4.0)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 40 90 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6b0c6971-bc61-5f21-bad2-d79ac11294ec")
	)
	(text "Everything left of the barrier is USB ground (DGND). The analog stage floats on AGND, which is the DUT minus terminal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 22.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(italic yes)
				(color 70 70 70 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f0dc54bd-8091-5232-92fc-89dcf10091c1")
	)
	(text "A   USB-C input: power, data, current advertisement (CC)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.5 33.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "576bb9b6-f6b2-5b28-bfd5-054c16717108")
	)
	(text "CC1 / CC2: 5.1k pull-downs = USB-C sink (UFP). The MCU reads the CC voltage to learn the source limit:\n0.4 V = 500 mA (legacy / USB 2.0 source), 0.9 V = 1.5 A, 1.7 V = 3 A. Below 1.5 A the firmware keeps the fan slow and limits power to 55 W.\nShield to DGND directly: the enclosure, if metal, is on the USB side. The DUT terminals and heatsink hardware must not touch it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 123 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8764ad5a-3fc4-53a5-8e9f-3f035afb2ad1")
	)
	(text "B   Logic supply 3.3 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.5 33.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6a7480c2-8aa8-5e45-a5de-dc6e9f5f221e")
	)
	(text "USB budget at 5 V: analog supply 0.12 A, MCU + isolator 0.06 A, displays up to 0.15 A, fan 0.45 A = 0.8 A.\nNeeds a 1.5 A or 3 A USB-C source for 150 W (fan). A 500 mA source still runs everything but the fan."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163 73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7e253d27-3ced-5040-ba17-b7d118791330")
	)
	(text "C   Fan supply: 5 V to 12 V boost, high-side switch, 4-pin PWM fan"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.5 91.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7fe378fa-6f45-5812-bfcb-8b02752966d6")
	)
	(text "Vout = 0.6 V x (1 + 191k / 10k) = 12.06 V. 12 V at 0.3 A costs about 0.8 A from USB.\nEN low: the boost stops and the output sits at VBUS minus a diode (4.7 V); Q1 is then off, so the fan sees nothing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163 196 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "104ce97d-8bf4-5abe-8ce3-c6646de725c5")
	)
	(text "J2 follows the 4-pin PC fan standard: 1 GND, 2 +12 V, 3 tach (open collector, pulled to 3.3 V here), 4 PWM 25 kHz.\n2- and 3-wire fans use pins 1-3 and are on/off only. Q3 drives the PWM pin open-drain, so firmware inverts the duty cycle.\nR11 only for fans without an internal PWM pull-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 255 208 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f97f1f16-5721-5b3d-8adb-3cc7a3886fa9")
	)
	(text "D   Isolated analog supply: 1 W DC-DC, 12 V filtered rail, 5 V reference rail"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.5 138.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9d5ad2f8-3227-52ad-94d1-5e02bfe5f2ff")
	)
	(text "BARRIER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.5 228 90)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
				(color 200 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4a224e2d-47ff-5702-93b9-c3c67b524735")
	)
	(text "PS1: unregulated. 12 V at full load, up to about 14 V at the 30 mA this board draws. Every part on +12V_ISO is rated 16 V or more.\nR12 / C8 filter the 100 kHz switching ripple (fc = 1.5 kHz) before it reaches the op-amps.\n+5V_ISO (MCP1703, 0.4 % typ) feeds the DAC and ADC logic and every threshold network. OTP, dropout, NTC-open and\nOVP thresholds are divider ratios of this same rail, so they do not depend on its absolute value.\nVERIFY the SIP-4 pin numbers of the DC-DC you buy before ordering the PCB (Mornsun and Murata differ)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 237.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1cdb3ac0-c160-557d-9204-3130390f8d20")
	)
	(text "E   Ground star point"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.5 225.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b8a0268b-a9ba-50ae-a55f-83ef553ae43c")
	)
	(text "AGND (analog reference) meets PGND (DUT minus, source resistors) ONLY at NT1.\nPlace NT1 at the centre of the four Rs bottom pads: 1 mR between an Rs and NT1 is 10 mV at 10 A,\n4 % of the 256 mV set-point full scale."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163 262 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e409585f-faa2-5ccb-a342-33455d6c594a")
	)
	(text "Isolation: USB side (DGND) to analog side (AGND / PGND). Working voltage rating of this barrier: 150 V DC\n(IEC 60664-1 functional, PD2, material group IIIb: 1.6 mm creepage; IPC-2221B B2: 0.7 mm). Board rule: 4 mm.\nISO7761 (5 kVrms, 8 mm) and the 3 kVDC DC-DC exceed it by far. Use it to float the load on a DUT referenced anywhere\nwithin 150 V of earth, not for mains-referenced work."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 285 232 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "788bc291-8d48-5a82-9c00-e4a064d71208")
	)
